# Governance Copilot — Steps 5 to 10 Run Guide

Everything below assumes you've already done Steps 1-4 (you have) and that
your terminal is open inside the `governance-copilot` folder.

---

## Step 5 — Build & test the agent pipeline

### 5.1 Install the new dependencies
```
pip install langgraph groq python-dotenv pypdf
```

### 5.2 Get your free Groq API key (if you haven't already)
1. Go to console.groq.com and sign up.
2. Left sidebar → API Keys → Create API Key.
3. Copy it — it's shown only once.

### 5.3 Set up your .env file
1. In the project folder, make a copy of `.env.example` and rename the copy to exactly `.env` (no ".example").
2. Open `.env` in VS Code and replace `paste_your_key_here` with your real key.
3. Save. **Never share this file or paste the key into chat with me** — it's your private credential.

### 5.4 Test the pieces that DON'T need the API key yet
```
python3 nodes_ingest_retrieve.py
```
This should print `[Ingest]` and `[Retrieve]` lines with real results — same as the retrieval test you already ran, just now wrapped as proper pipeline nodes.

```
python3 nodes_validate.py
```
This runs a self-test with fake data and should end with:
```
Self-test PASSED — the hard gate correctly separated real evidence from invented evidence.
```
This is the single most important line in the entire project — it proves the tool cannot silently make up compliance claims.

### 5.5 Test the pieces that DO need the API key
```
python3 nodes_map.py
```
This actually calls the AI model for the first time. Should print several `[control_id] title — SATISFIED / not satisfied` lines.

```
python3 nodes_report.py
```
Runs the whole chain and prints a full written gap report at the end.

### 5.6 Run the whole pipeline as one unit
```
python3 agent.py
```
This is Step 5, complete — one command runs Ingest → Retrieve → Map → Validate → Report and prints the final report.

**If anything errors here, stop and tell me the exact error before moving on — don't skip ahead if this step doesn't work cleanly.**

