## Step 9 — Deploy for free

1. Create a free GitHub account if you don't have one (github.com).
2. Create a new repository, e.g. `governance-copilot`.
3. Push your project folder to it (VS Code has a built-in "Source Control" tab that can do this with a few clicks — ask me for the click-by-click if you want it).
4. **Double-check `.env` is NOT in what you're pushing** — the `.gitignore` file already excludes it, but visually confirm on GitHub after pushing that your real API key isn't visible anywhere in the repo.
5. Go to streamlit.io/cloud, sign in with GitHub, click "New app," point it at your repo and `app.py`.
6. In the app's settings on Streamlit Cloud, add a "Secret" named `GROQ_API_KEY` with your real key — this is the cloud equivalent of your local `.env` file.
7. Deploy. You'll get a public URL you can put on your resume/LinkedIn.

